{"authored" [{"question" "q-10076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=9 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f5c55c1dee1ff993ca21ac73c69c34ef9fcc84fd77e4a3a4dae51e796de9e62" "basis" 1789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ -49 \\\\ -58\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=19,y=-49,z=-58.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f5c55c1dee1ff993ca21ac73c69c34ef9fcc84fd77e4a3a4dae51e796de9e62" "basis" 1789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0b4508c62d22a564eb9e31f54d4e8f6f7eaab04b149df88ec838b0bdcc088bba" "basis" 1789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-worker